To resolve the issue of counting the number of cookies set in your MooTools-based to-do list application and reading their values, you can utilize the `document.cookie` property. Here's how to approach the problem:

1. **Counting the Cookies**: You can access `document.cookie`, which contains all cookies for the current document as a single string, delimited by semicolons. To count the cookies, you can split this string and get the length of the resulting array.

2. **Looping Through the Cookies**: Once you have the cookies as an array, you can loop through each cookie to read its value.

3. **Modify Your Code**: Here's an example of how you might modify your existing code to count and read the cookies:

```javascript
window.addEvent('domready', function() {
    $('add').addEvent('click', function() {
        var value = $('todo').value;
        var t = new Todo(value, "beschrijving", new Date(), 1);
        var storeData = JSON.encode(t);

        Cookie.write(value, storeData, {duration: 1});

        // Reading all cookies
        var allCookies = document.cookie.split(';');
        console.log("Number of cookies: " + allCookies.length);

        allCookies.forEach(function(cookie) {
            var cookiePair = cookie.split('=');
            var cookieName = cookiePair[0].trim();
            var cookieValue = cookiePair[1];
            console.log("Cookie Name: " + cookieName + ", Value: " + cookieValue);
        });
    });
});

var Todo = new Class({
    initialize: function(title, description, date, isDone) {
        this.title = title;
        this.description = description;
        this.date = new Date();
        this.isDone = isDone;
    },

    getTitle: function() {
        return this.title;
    },

    getIsDone: function() {
        return this.isDone;
    },

    setIsDone: function(value) {
        this.isDone = value;
    },
});
```

### Key Changes:
- **Use `document.cookie`**: This accesses all cookies as a string which you can split using `;` to get individual cookies.
- **Count and Loop Through Cookies**: The resulting array allows you to count cookies and extract their name and value.

This approach will provide you with the functionality you're looking for—counting and retrieving your cookie values in the MooTools application.

