<ul>
<li>add that new username/password combination to your MySQL server, logging in from phpmyadmin with the old username to do that. <a href="https://pureinfotech.com/install-xampp-windows-10/#change_phpmyadmin_password_xampp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Here's a suggestion about that</a>.</li>
<li>update your db.inc.php file or whatever in your php application gives the username/password.</li>
</ul>

<p>Your php program <em>logs in to MySQL</em>. MySQL is server software that happens to be running on your local machine when you use xampp. So both it and MySQL must agree on a username

